WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.610
One thing that came up in these stories today

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.330
that I really thought was interesting,

3
00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.720
and I'd love to get your take on, everybody,

4
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.434
is we're gonna talk about spoilers.

5
00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.890
Now I just assumed everyone hates a spoiler.

6
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.830
It turns out some people love them.

7
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.190
The Washington Post reports

8
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.190
that some people wanna know how a TV show ends

9
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.550
before they watch it.

10
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:23.570
Or they like to read that last page of the book

11
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.510
before they buy it.

12
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.180 line:15%
Very "When Harry Met Sally."

13
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.890 line:15%
They say spoilers help them determine

14
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.360 line:15%
if they wanna invest the time

15
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.100 line:15%
in a TV show, movie, book.

16
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.020 line:15%
And for some, knowing the outcome

17
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.260 line:15%
helps them enjoy the ride even more.

18
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.840 line:15%
Ross, thoughts?

19
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.887 line:15%
Well, you know, I don't like to judge anybody.

20
00:00:38.887 --> 00:00:40.101 line:15%
(Drew laughs)

21
00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:41.690 line:15%
But something is seriously wrong with you.

22
00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.560 line:15%
(audience laughs)

23
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.440 line:15%
I don't like you, I don't know you.

24
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.350 line:15%
I don't wanna know you.

25
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.183 line:15%
What? Why?

26
00:00:47.183 --> 00:00:48.900 line:15%
Why would you wanna know how it ends?

27
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.320 line:15%
Why would you wanna know that Carrie

28
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.153 line:15%
ended up with Big?

29
00:00:51.153 --> 00:00:52.118 line:15%
Sorry, if you didn't know.

30
00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.543 line:15%
(audience laughs)

31
00:00:53.543 --> 00:00:54.620 line:15%
Why would you wanna know that

32
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.830 line:15%
and not go on the journey of the character?

33
00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.331 line:15%
You need help. I'm sorry, but you do.

34
00:00:59.331 --> 00:01:00.164 line:15%
(audience laughs)

35
00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:01.750 line:15%
Okay, show of hands,

36
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.310 line:15%
who likes spoilers in the audience?

37
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.304
Now listen.
(audience laughs)

38
00:01:08.304 --> 00:01:10.320
You looked so normal to me, sitting there.

39
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.160
(audience laughs)

40
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.810
I see a woman right here in the front row.

41
00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.380
What is your name?

42
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.740
And why did you raise your hand?

43
00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.990
My name is Karina,

44
00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.190
and when I go to the book store

45
00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.590
and pick up a book, I always go to the ending.

46
00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:25.970
If I don't like the ending,

47
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.930
I don't buy the book.

48
00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.940
Now listen, you seem normal to me, right?

49
00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.910
You do.
(audience laughs)

50
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.400
But don't you wanna go on the journey, dear?

51
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.330
Don't you wanna, you know, find out,

52
00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.610
and see what happens?

53
00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.090
Yeah, but the ending of the book

54
00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.540
tells me whether or not the journey

55
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.323
is going to be worth reading the rest of the book.

56
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.580
You know...
(audience laughs)

57
00:01:50.487 --> 00:01:51.640
And then like, TV series.

58
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.660
Like, if I find out a TV series is being canceled

59
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.493
that I'm watching,

60
00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:55.710
I'm just like, I just drop it.

61
00:01:57.151 --> 00:01:59.984
(audience laughs)

62
00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.180
I'm sorry to disappoint you!

63
00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.750
Well, you'll be happy to know "Yellowstone"

64
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.210
just got picked up for season five.

65
00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.130
I know, season five!
(audience applauds)

66
00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:10.334
I've been binging all weekends.

67
00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:11.540
All weekends.

68
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:12.860
Thank you for participating!

69
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.080
Thank you, I still don't get you.

70
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.310
But thank you.
(audience laughs)

71
00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.410
I love that we can learn from each other.

72
00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.940
All right, next up,

73
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.300
do you wanna know what the end of this story is

74
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.406
before I get to it?

75
00:02:24.406 --> 00:02:25.435
(audience laughs)

76
00:02:25.435 --> 00:02:26.270
All right, next up-

77
00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.100
Now I kind of wanna try it.

78
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.650
Okay, scroll to the last line.

79
00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.260
I'll give you the last line.
Yeah, do it!

80
00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.532
Do it, scroll to the end, ready?

81
00:02:33.532 --> 00:02:34.365
Dan, will you go to the end?

82
00:02:34.365 --> 00:02:35.198
Here are the last line.

83
00:02:35.198 --> 00:02:37.555
Instead, why not give the bride a hand?

84
00:02:37.555 --> 00:02:40.388
(audience laughs)

85
00:02:41.695 --> 00:02:44.617
(audience applauds)

86
00:02:44.617 --> 00:02:45.460
Okay, back to the top, let's try this.

87
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.180
We're talking about the wedding term

88
00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.130
that some experts say we have to retire.

89
00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.766
Anybody ever heard of the term bridezilla?

90
00:02:52.766 --> 00:02:53.839
(audience mutters)

91
00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:54.672
Uh-huh.

92
00:02:54.672 --> 00:02:55.505
Well, Insider reports that term was coined

93
00:02:55.505 --> 00:02:56.338
way back in the 90's,

94
00:02:56.338 --> 00:02:57.580
and it's been thrown about so much,

95
00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.250
but it is actually unfair.

96
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.030
Because they say planning a wedding

97
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.220
really is stressful and is emotional,

98
00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.950 line:15%
and we don't need to demonize women

99
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.720 line:15%
who are just trying to pull together a big day

100
00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.040 line:15%
under a ton of pressure.

101
00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.500 line:15%
Instead, they say,

102
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.441 line:15%
why not give that bride a hand?

103
00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:12.890 line:15%
(Drew laughs)

104
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.670 line:15%
Why not give the bride a hand?

105
00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.690 line:15%
I tell you, I'm in the middle

106
00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.190 line:15%
of planning a wedding right now,

107
00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.770 line:15%
and I am not groomzilla.

108
00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:19.603 line:15%
Okay?

109
00:03:19.603 --> 00:03:21.570 line:15%
I was maybe in a moment or two...

110
00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.320
Not even in the neighborhood of groomzilla,

111
00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.153
but the area code.

112
00:03:24.153 --> 00:03:25.808
Kind of like, a moment of stress.

113
00:03:25.808 --> 00:03:26.641
(audience laughs)

114
00:03:26.641 --> 00:03:29.001
And just yesterday they did a face time,

115
00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:31.090
like, at the venue of where it's gonna be,

116
00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.650
and something in my head clicked

117
00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:33.620
and it was all gone.

118
00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.440
You know, all the stress was gone.

119
00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.273
Really?

120
00:03:36.273 --> 00:03:37.400
Yeah, and I think there should be that moment.

121
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.650
I hope there's that moment for every bride,

122
00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.483
every groom out there,

123
00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:40.860
every person who's having a wedding,

124
00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.270
where you do get to let go of that.

125
00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.000
Because it is so stressful.

126
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.180
And to demonize people who are

127
00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.520
just trying to have a moment is wrong.

128
00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.210
This one made me feel bad about the term.

129
00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.700
I was like, "Yeah, you're right."

130
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.270
Like, if you're really going through it,

131
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.190
and you got a ton of pressure,

132
00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.390
and all that stuff,

133
00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.720
the last thing you need is someone giving you

134
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.860
a rude nickname that's gonna make you

135
00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:04.430
feel worse about yourself.

136
00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.880
Yeah, how about we just don't judge people

137
00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.210
who are just trying to express love?

138
00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.301
How about that?

139
00:04:08.301 --> 00:04:09.770
Right?
(audience applauds)

140
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.540
We could do that.

141
00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.560
I like how everybody likes to do it,

142
00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.640
and they should be supported

143
00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.150
and not be called some ratty little name for it.

144
00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.105
We'll be right back.

145
00:04:18.105 --> 00:04:20.343 line:15%
(upbeat music)
Yeah, do it your way.

